# xwayland-satellite v0.8.2 pins `time` 0.3.44, vulnerable to
# GHSA-r6v5-fh4h-64xc (fixed 0.3.47). `time` is not a direct dependency —
# pulled in transitively via the `vergen-gitcl` build-dependency. Bumps
# Cargo.lock's `time` entry (and the transitive deps that moved with it:
# deranged, num-conv, time-core, time-macros; drops itoa/serde, which
# time no longer needs at this version) to 0.3.55, the newest published
# release that is not yanked (0.3.48 and 0.3.50 both are) — produced via
# `cargo update -p time --precise 0.3.55` against the v0.8.2 tag.
#
# Verified locally: `cargo build --release --locked` with this Cargo.lock
# compiles vergen-gitcl + time + xwayland-satellite itself cleanly under
# rustc 1.98.0 (time 0.3.55's MSRV is 1.88.0; freedesktop-sdk's
# components/rust.bst ships 1.98.0, well above it). The only local build
# failure was xcb-util-cursor-sys needing pkg-config, unrelated to this
# bump and satisfied in the BST sandbox by components/pkg-config.bst.
#
# Remove once upstream's own Cargo.lock carries `time` >= 0.3.47.

